{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Ce4mSAk7ax7v7qCMFjGCV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Placement Decision\n\n**Where to add it:**\n\n```markdown\n## 2. Failure handling\n\n- **Retries are bounded and jittered.** Every retry wrapper declares\n  its maximum attempt count at the call site; backoff is exponential\n  with jitter, and a non-retriable error class aborts immediately —\n  enumerate those classes beside the wrapper, not in a distant\n  constants file.\n- **Timeouts are explicit.** No call inherits a library default\n  timeout silently; the call site states its per-attempt timeout.\n  A retry wrapper must cap total elapsed time in addition to per-attempt\n  timeout, since a per-attempt timeout with unbounded attempts still\n  hangs the caller; declare both the attempt cap and the wall-clock cap\n  at the call site.\n```\n\n## Explanation\n\nThe new rule belongs in §2 (Failure handling), and within that section it is a natural extension of the existing \"Timeouts are explicit\" bullet. That bullet already owns the topic of timeout declaration at the call site; the new rule strengthens it by forbidding a common incomplete pattern (per-attempt timeout without wall-clock timeout). Rather than create a standalone third bullet, I folded the rule into the host bullet as a trailing clause, since it clarifies and reinforces the same principle already stated there."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":645,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":300,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
